 {"sec": "Resistant shock branches and ECMO · p258", "page": 258, "q": "Match each resistant-shock scenario with its management:", "opts": ["A-2, B-4, C-3, D-1", "A-1, B-4, C-2, D-3", "A-2, B-4, C-1, D-3", "A-4, B-2, C-1, D-3"], "ans": 2, "exp": "BP status splits cold-shock therapy; failure leads to reversible causes and ECMO. Correct pairs: Cold with normal BP→Vasodilators nitroprusside and nitroglycerin; Cold with low BP→Epi highest plus norepi for diastolic; Warm with low BP→Volume plus vasopressin; No response→Reversible causes then ECMO. (Book p258)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["Cold with normal BP", "Volume plus vasopressin"], ["Cold with low BP", "Vasodilators nitroprusside and nitroglycerin"], ["Warm with low BP", "Reversible causes then ECMO"], ["No response", "Epi highest plus norepi for diastolic"]], "id": "PEDS-C54-122"},
